Z||000008||Songman||06-12-2001||02:21 AM||||I love the Firebird wing on my T-top.. sits lower and flatter than the stock Fiero wing. And you can find them for about $20 in junk yards sometimes. I knew a guy that bought one at a swap meet recently for $5! Did he ever get it finished, Spidey?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||AusFiero||06-12-2001||07:37 AM||||Any third generation Firbird wing will work, width wise anyway. A friend has  a 3rd gen with a Fiero wing on it...looks like it was mean't to be there.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
